**ABSTRACT**

A wireless power and data transmission system (10) and method for simultaneously delivering electrical energy and communicating telemetry are disclosed. The method comprises the steps of: 

a) acquiring at least one analog signal ($AD_x$) via a sensor interface (12); 

b) digitizing the analog signal ($AD_x$) into a stream of binary digital bits ($D_x$) using an analog-to-digital converter (14); 

c) establishing operational bound parameters comprising a minimum event limit ($n_{min}$) and a maximum event limit ($n_{max}$) within a system controller (16); 

d) mapping the binary digital bits ($D_x$) to discrete high/low event counts comprising a low event count ($n_{low}$) and a high event count ($n_{high}$), wherein $n_{low}$ and $n_{high}$ are derived within the range defined by $n_{min}$ and $n_{max}$; 

e) modulating a high-frequency power carrier signal generated by a driver circuit (18) according to the mapped low event count ($n_{low}$) and high event count ($n_{high}$); 

f) wirelessly transmitting the modulated carrier signal across an inductive coupling link via a primary coil assembly (20); 

g) capturing the transmitted carrier signal at a secondary receiver circuit (22); 

h) harvesting operational power from the captured carrier signal to energize a local system load (24); 

i) demodulating the captured carrier signal by counting high and low pulse transitions to reconstruct the event counts ($n_{low}$, $n_{high}$) evaluated against $n_{min}$ and $n_{max}$ using a demodulator circuit (26); and 

j) reconstructing the binary digital bits ($D_x$) and synthesizing the original analog signal ($AD_x$) at a processing unit (28) for downstream execution.
